        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Using the `main` branch of any project is a pretty poor advice. Even though yours might work I am not going to hunt my plugins across main branches of various projects and be dealing with random breakage. The release concept exists for a reason.\n\nNobody was advising to use `main` for any project. The documentation on the site is generated for `main` branch and it is explicitly mentions that.\n\nYou are free to use whichever version you prefer. To get the documentation of your installed version, use `:h mini.clue` from inside Neovim session. It does not contain array `mode` in the examples.\n\n> Your expectation of users quickly figuring things out from large amount of documentation text is wrong, it takes time and you add to the wasted time by increasing the confusion like this.\n\nMy expectation from the users is that they are able to read, understand, and follow the documentation.",
