        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Nobody was advising to use main for any project.\n\nThat's how I understood this sentence:\n\n> This setup describes how main branch works and there is no issues using it.\n\nThen if `main` is not intended to be used, why expose the documentation for it.\n\n> ... use :h mini.clue from inside Neovim session ...\n\nPartially fair I guess (at least in this case), but when setting up a plugin one has to read the documentation first to get it running in neovim to be able to view that doc in the first place. Pretty orthogonal to actually having the relevant doc on the web (since you even have a dedicated website for it).",
