        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> > Nobody was advising to use main for any project.\n> \n> That's how I understood this sentence:\n> \n> > This setup describes how main branch works and there is no issues using it.\n> \n> Then if `main` is not intended to be used, why expose the documentation for it.\n\nNobody said that the `main` is not intended to be used either. There are exactly two facts:\n- Documentation on the nvim-mini.org website is generated for the `main` branch. It explicitly says so.\n- Documentation on the site is correct for the `main` branch.\n\nNothing more, nothing less. It was mostly a reaction to \"Here I am wondering why the hell I'm getting tracebacks.\" (it is for `main` and works if using `main`).\n\nAs per Neovim plugins, I usually do indeed find that using their default branch is good enough and easier. This is what [MiniMax](https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax) uses as well.\n\n---\n\nEverything here works as expected and will continue to work how it currently does.",
